# Basic Heatmap

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`Heatmap.new(z: [[...]])` renders a 2D matrix as a colour-encoded grid.
Each inner list is a row. The default colour scale maps low values to blue
and high values to red (`"RdBu"` reversed, or the default Plotly scale).

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Heatmap}

z = [
  [1,  20, 30],
  [20, 1,  60],
  [30, 60, 1 ]
]

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Heatmap.new(z: z))
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Basic Heatmap")
|> Plotly.show()
```
